  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High level reclamation forum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The economic section of the Netherlands embassy in Jakarta, Indonesia, wishes to promote Dutch infrastructure companies in Indonesia, focussing on sustainability towards land reclamation. The Dutch reclamation sector has an excellent reputation worldwide, except in Indonesia. The Netherlands embassy and the Indonesia Netherlands Association (INA) would like to cooperate to counter the negative publicity concerning reclamations in Indonesia and promote Dutch knowledge and competencies, especially about sustainable manners of reclamation.The Netherlands embassy plans to host a high-level seminar for the Indonesian government and local stakeholders with approximately 250 attendees. This event will take place during the Indonesia International Infrastructure Exhibition.The forum aims to inform the Indonesian (local) government(s) about sustainable manners of reclamation and how Dutch companies could be involved since sustainable reclamation is a Dutch speciality. In addition, the seminar will promote governmental measures for sustainable reclamation, such as conducting environmental impact assessments and adapting rules and regulations in favour of sustainable reclamation. These measures are crucial to ensure sustainable reclamation practices and will be highlighted during the seminar.</narrative>
  </description>
